                    <li><h3>Enhance university assets</h3><p>Develop natural and economic resources, facilities, and expertise.</p></li>
                    <li><h3>Learn through experience</h3><p>Provide faculty, staff, students, and stakeholders with hands-on training venues and opportunities to earn while they learn.</p></li>
                    <li><h3>Share knowledge and records</h3><p>Provide instruction, research, and extension materials through recorded statistics on crops, livestock, forest products, and natural resources.</p></li>
                    <li><h3>Support laboratory needs</h3><p>Provide or augment livestock, crops, and other materials within RGMO programs for students and researchers.</p></li>
                    <li><h3>Build collaborative partnerships</h3><p>Establish linkages with SUCs and public, private, and community partners for collaborative activities.</p></li>
                </ol>
